# Hooks Directory

Place custom scripts here to run before or after a resource is updated.

## Naming Convention

    <CTID>-pre.sh     Runs INSIDE the container BEFORE apt/docker updates
    <CTID>-post.sh    Runs INSIDE the container AFTER apt/docker updates

## Examples

Stop a service before upgrading, restart after:

    # File: 108-pre.sh
    systemctl stop plexmediaserver

    # File: 108-post.sh
    systemctl start plexmediaserver

Run a custom update command for a service:

    # File: 119-post.sh
    cd /opt/n8n && npm update -g n8n

## Security

Hook files must be owned by root and must NOT be group- or world-writable.
The script will skip any hook that fails this check and log a warning.

    chown root:root hooks/*.sh
    chmod 700 hooks/*.sh

Note: Hooks currently only work for LXC containers (executed via pct exec).
